course: dictionary
lesson: 9184
title: Sober: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word sober is a good example. Its meaning changes with the words around it, so the context tells you which meaning the writer chose.
explain: «Drivers must be sober.» Here sober means not drunk, not affected by alcohol. The rest of the sentence gives the clue: drivers need clear heads to keep everyone safe on the road.
explain: «The sober colours of the old coat were brown and grey.» Here sober means plain and dull, not bright. «A sober reminder» is different again: it means something that makes people stop and think seriously. Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence, then test your meaning.
explain: In the Bible, «think of yourself with sober judgment» (Romans 12:3) means thinking clearly, honestly and sensibly, without being carried away. When a word has several meanings, read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Sober means not drunk, not affected by alcohol.
fact: Sober also means serious, calm and sensible, as in «a sober mood».
fact: Sober colours or clothes are plain and dull, not bright.
fact: To sober up means to stop being drunk. «Sobering thought» means a thought that makes you serious.
fact: Some words have several meanings, so always check the context before you choose one.
exercise: What does sober mean in «Drivers must be sober»? | *Not drunk, not affected by alcohol | Angry with other drivers | Very tired after a long day | Quite cheerful
exercise: «The sober colours of the old coat were brown and grey.» What does sober mean here? | Shiny and new | *Plain and dull, not bright | Soft and warm | Bright and loud
exercise: «The news gave a sober reminder that we must all wear seatbelts.» What does sober mean here? | *Serious, making people stop and think | Funny and silly | Very fast
test: Which phrase means to stop being drunk? | sober reminder | sober colours | *sober up | sober judgment
test: In «think of yourself with sober judgment», what does sober judgment mean? | Angry and loud guessing | *Clear, honest and sensible thinking | Hurried, with no thought at all
exam: Read: «Do not think of yourself more highly than you ought, but rather think of yourself with sober judgment.» What does the sentence ask us to be? | Lazy and tired | Proud and loud | Bright and colourful | *Clear, honest and sensible
